WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.292 --> 00:00:07.337
How do you start a new city?

00:00:08.547 --> 00:00:11.132
Turns out it's not easy.

00:00:11.633 --> 00:00:13.218
You need to survey terrain,

00:00:13.260 --> 00:00:15.762
get permission from a state, buy land,

00:00:15.804 --> 00:00:17.514
convince people to move there.

00:00:18.223 --> 00:00:21.351
And until Elon Musk gets us to Mars,

00:00:21.351 --> 00:00:23.395
land is a finite resource.

00:00:23.853 --> 00:00:26.523
And the good spots are probably all taken.

00:00:28.441 --> 00:00:32.487
But what if we could start smaller,
like really small?

00:00:33.029 --> 00:00:34.739
And just post on Twitter.

00:00:36.575 --> 00:00:37.742
That's what I did,

00:00:37.784 --> 00:00:40.370
because it allowed me
to find people all over the world

00:00:40.412 --> 00:00:42.038
willing to help me figure it out.

00:00:42.581 --> 00:00:45.375
My new internet friends and I
started a group chat,

00:00:45.417 --> 00:00:47.002
pooled cryptocurrency,

00:00:47.002 --> 00:00:48.628
researched locations,

00:00:48.670 --> 00:00:50.255
and three months later,

00:00:50.297 --> 00:00:52.674
we bought 40 acres of land

00:00:52.716 --> 00:00:55.510
near Yellowstone National Park in Wyoming.

00:00:57.095 --> 00:01:01.433
Now we had a piece of land,
a pool of money,

00:01:01.474 --> 00:01:04.311
and a lot of decisions
to make collectively.

00:01:05.895 --> 00:01:09.024
That’s why we decided to start a DAO,

00:01:09.065 --> 00:01:14.696
or a decentralized autonomous
organization, called CityDAO.

00:01:15.530 --> 00:01:19.743
A DAO is an internet native,
blockchain-governed,

00:01:19.784 --> 00:01:24.623
collectively owned organization
working towards a shared mission.

00:01:25.457 --> 00:01:28.501
Most DAOs pool
cryptocurrency in a treasury

00:01:28.543 --> 00:01:30.754
where members vote on how it's used.

00:01:32.756 --> 00:01:34.007
In a traditional company,

00:01:34.049 --> 00:01:38.553
a CEO works with executives
to set the direction, the budgets

00:01:38.553 --> 00:01:41.723
and hands priorities down
the org chart to be implemented.

00:01:42.682 --> 00:01:46.227
In a DAO, members act as peers,

00:01:46.269 --> 00:01:47.729
contributing capital,

00:01:47.771 --> 00:01:49.731
proposing and working on projects

00:01:49.773 --> 00:01:52.108
and making decisions as a group.

00:01:52.692 --> 00:01:57.656
Top-down management is replaced
by blockchain-based rules

00:01:57.697 --> 00:01:59.824
encoded in smart contracts.

00:01:59.866 --> 00:02:03.912
For example, funding a project
if a proposal passes.

00:02:06.122 --> 00:02:07.957
If a traditional company succeeds,

00:02:07.999 --> 00:02:11.127
most of the wealth will accrue
to a few founders,

00:02:11.169 --> 00:02:12.545
some early employees

00:02:12.587 --> 00:02:15.507
and investors who are generally
already higher net-worth.

00:02:15.799 --> 00:02:18.426
A DAO is a sort of crypto co-op,

00:02:18.468 --> 00:02:22.222
giving a wider group of people
the opportunity to own a piece,

00:02:22.263 --> 00:02:24.099
participate in management

00:02:24.140 --> 00:02:27.018
and share in the potential upside.

00:02:28.561 --> 00:02:33.483
CityDAO grew out of my frustrations
dealing with city bureaucracy and red tape

00:02:33.525 --> 00:02:34.734
while building a start-up

00:02:34.776 --> 00:02:37.612
that helps cities better utilize
their empty parking lots.

00:02:38.780 --> 00:02:40.156
It took us over three months

00:02:40.156 --> 00:02:42.701
to get a permit just to sell
parking in San Francisco.

00:02:42.701 --> 00:02:45.453
And it was an archaic
bureaucratic nightmare.

00:02:46.663 --> 00:02:49.457
Things like putting a parking lot
to higher and better use,

00:02:49.457 --> 00:02:53.378
which my urbanist self really wants to do,
like, you know, build a food truck park,

00:02:53.378 --> 00:02:55.338
logistics hub, maybe even new housing,

00:02:55.380 --> 00:02:56.506
a farmer's market.

00:02:56.548 --> 00:02:59.843
These things are also really tedious,
can take months, years,

00:02:59.884 --> 00:03:02.220
or even just be illegal
due to zoning laws.

00:03:03.680 --> 00:03:06.683
CityDAO was among the first DAOs
brave enough to buy land.

00:03:07.350 --> 00:03:10.895
And speaking of bureaucracy,
it took us over a month to do so

00:03:10.937 --> 00:03:12.439
under the current system.

00:03:12.480 --> 00:03:14.691
We had to find an agent, coordinate tours,

00:03:14.733 --> 00:03:16.484
make offers, wait for counteroffers,

00:03:16.484 --> 00:03:17.819
put down a deposit,

00:03:17.861 --> 00:03:19.404
form an LLC, fill out paperwork.

00:03:19.946 --> 00:03:23.408
At CityDAO, we imagine an on-chain city

00:03:23.408 --> 00:03:25.410
where things like permitting, budgets,

00:03:25.452 --> 00:03:27.287
laws, deeds and records,

00:03:27.328 --> 00:03:29.456
they're all just transparent
on a blockchain,

00:03:29.456 --> 00:03:32.250
and smart contracts
can speed up the transactions

00:03:32.292 --> 00:03:33.960
and reduce bureaucracy.

00:03:34.377 --> 00:03:35.670
Let me give you an example.

00:03:35.670 --> 00:03:37.547
Things that used to take weeks,

00:03:37.547 --> 00:03:39.549
like buying or selling land

00:03:39.591 --> 00:03:42.218
or taking a loan out
against your property,

00:03:42.260 --> 00:03:45.513
that could happen in seconds
through a smart contract.

00:03:49.225 --> 00:03:53.104
DAOs are financial flash mobs,

00:03:53.146 --> 00:03:57.192
often organizing seemingly overnight
in pursuit of an idea.

00:03:57.567 --> 00:04:00.403
They usually start out
as a few people who have a big vision

00:04:00.403 --> 00:04:03.740
but realize it will take a large
collective effort to get it done.

00:04:06.743 --> 00:04:09.537
So they usually start the community
in a group chat server,

00:04:09.537 --> 00:04:11.372
and the most common is called Discord.

00:04:11.372 --> 00:04:13.333
We use Discord for weekly community calls

00:04:13.333 --> 00:04:15.919
where people can share ideas
and debate proposals.

00:04:16.544 --> 00:04:20.048
In the server, channels are set up
around teams and projects.

00:04:20.048 --> 00:04:21.758
Instead of a formal boss,

00:04:21.800 --> 00:04:25.512
each team has an elected facilitator
who holds regular meetings.

00:04:26.846 --> 00:04:30.266
People can contribute to the DAO
full-time, part-time,

00:04:30.308 --> 00:04:32.769
but one of the most common ways
is through bounties,

00:04:32.769 --> 00:04:34.521
where you hop in and out of the DAO,

00:04:34.562 --> 00:04:37.190
taking on small tasks
and contributing where you can.

00:04:39.150 --> 00:04:43.029
Most DAOs raised some initial funding
by selling a governance token

00:04:43.029 --> 00:04:46.241
that gives holders voting rights
over DAO activities.

00:04:46.866 --> 00:04:49.244
You can either buy these tokens
on the open market

00:04:49.285 --> 00:04:51.871
using a cryptocurrency like Ethereum,

00:04:51.913 --> 00:04:54.541
or you can earn them
by contributing to the DAO.

00:04:54.582 --> 00:04:58.503
For example, things like designing a logo,
researching or writing some code.

00:05:00.296 --> 00:05:03.091
At CityDAO, we raised
over six million dollars

00:05:03.132 --> 00:05:07.220
from 5,000 people through our
governance token called “Citizenship”.

00:05:07.262 --> 00:05:09.138
Citizens get to vote in things like

00:05:09.180 --> 00:05:11.432
where our next piece
of land will be located.

00:05:11.808 --> 00:05:15.395
DAOs have been called group chats
with a bank account.

00:05:16.688 --> 00:05:18.231
And I know what you're thinking.

00:05:18.231 --> 00:05:20.984
"Scott, sharing a bank account
with my significant other

00:05:21.025 --> 00:05:22.235
is already hard enough.

00:05:22.235 --> 00:05:25.905
Now you're telling me I have to share one
with 5,000 people on the internet?"

00:05:27.156 --> 00:05:29.492
Well, it's not that bad.

00:05:29.492 --> 00:05:31.160
Blockchain helps fix this.

00:05:31.202 --> 00:05:35.039
So funds live in a public
blockchain treasury

00:05:35.039 --> 00:05:37.876
where anyone can audit
income and spending.

00:05:37.917 --> 00:05:40.670
And any time spending
or money transfers are involved,

00:05:40.712 --> 00:05:43.464
the DAO approves it through a proposal.

00:05:44.382 --> 00:05:46.551
Typically written by a DAO member,

00:05:46.593 --> 00:05:49.846
a proposal starts as an idea
that gets debated

00:05:49.888 --> 00:05:52.473
and is put to a vote of the token holders.

00:05:52.515 --> 00:05:53.683
For example,

00:05:53.725 --> 00:05:56.728
one of the first proposals
at CityDAO was, of course,

00:05:56.769 --> 00:05:58.479
which piece of land to buy.

00:05:59.814 --> 00:06:03.192
The DAO debated must-haves, nice-to-haves,

00:06:03.192 --> 00:06:07.280
and DAO contributors combed
through Wyoming land listings

00:06:07.322 --> 00:06:09.699
and narrowed it down to the top three,

00:06:09.699 --> 00:06:11.910
outlining the pros and cons of each

00:06:11.951 --> 00:06:15.705
and presenting the final proposal
to the DAO for a vote.

00:06:17.123 --> 00:06:21.753
We voted to acquire Parcel 0
near Cody, Wyoming.

00:06:22.462 --> 00:06:25.048
Chosen for being close to an airport,

00:06:25.089 --> 00:06:28.051
having an on-site well for water access,

00:06:28.092 --> 00:06:29.302
and of course,

00:06:29.344 --> 00:06:32.513
the most important criterion of all,

00:06:32.513 --> 00:06:34.223
being near Kanye West.

00:06:34.223 --> 00:06:35.266
(Laughter)

00:06:35.308 --> 00:06:37.727
OK, OK, that wasn't really
in the criteria,

00:06:37.727 --> 00:06:39.145
but it just so happens

00:06:39.187 --> 00:06:43.316
our piece of land in Wyoming
is not far from Kanye's own Cody ranch.

00:06:46.235 --> 00:06:47.445
The next steps at CityDAO

00:06:47.487 --> 00:06:49.989
are things like voting
on what gets built on the land

00:06:50.031 --> 00:06:51.616
and who gets to use it when.

00:06:52.575 --> 00:06:55.703
Some other proposals floating around

00:06:55.745 --> 00:06:59.874
are things like buying a piece of land
in the Amazon for conservation

00:06:59.874 --> 00:07:03.795
or building out a network
of DAO-owned spaces

00:07:03.795 --> 00:07:05.588
where citizens can visit at any time,

00:07:05.630 --> 00:07:07.924
a decentralized city, perhaps.

00:07:11.260 --> 00:07:15.765
Today we're seeing DAOs do all kinds
of really interesting things together.

00:07:15.807 --> 00:07:18.559
They're building products,
they're investing in start-ups,

00:07:18.601 --> 00:07:20.061
they're buying art and assets,

00:07:20.061 --> 00:07:22.397
they're funding research
and raising money.

00:07:22.689 --> 00:07:24.482
Let's take a look at some examples.

00:07:25.733 --> 00:07:30.947
ConstitutionDAO raised
over 47 million dollars in seven days

00:07:30.989 --> 00:07:34.200
in attempt to buy an original
US Constitution copy.

00:07:34.909 --> 00:07:38.538
It usually takes longer than seven days
just to set up a company

00:07:38.579 --> 00:07:39.914
and open a bank account.

00:07:40.540 --> 00:07:44.502
Krause House is buying an NBA team
and LinksDAO a golf course.

00:07:44.961 --> 00:07:47.672
DAO members will likely
get to participate in key things,

00:07:47.672 --> 00:07:50.883
like who's coaching the team
or where the golf course gets built.

00:07:51.801 --> 00:07:55.763
PleasrDAO collects art
and digital assets like NFTs.

00:07:56.639 --> 00:07:59.767
They recently purchased
the only copy in existence

00:07:59.767 --> 00:08:02.020
of an unreleased Wu-Tang Clan album,

00:08:02.061 --> 00:08:04.689
and DAO members are now
the only people in the world

00:08:04.731 --> 00:08:06.482
who can legally listen to it.

00:08:07.900 --> 00:08:10.570
VectorDAO is a collective of designers

00:08:10.611 --> 00:08:12.196
shaking up the agency model

00:08:12.196 --> 00:08:16.034
where DAO members get ownership
in each project they work on.

00:08:19.328 --> 00:08:22.707
In DAOs like MetaCartel and Seed Club,

00:08:22.707 --> 00:08:26.335
members review submissions
from promising start-ups and projects

00:08:26.377 --> 00:08:28.171
and decide on which ones to fund.

00:08:28.921 --> 00:08:30.965
VitaDAO is funding research,

00:08:31.007 --> 00:08:34.427
and more recently, UkraineDAO
raised over six million dollars

00:08:34.469 --> 00:08:36.929
to donate towards
the Ukrainian defense effort.

00:08:40.349 --> 00:08:42.643
It’s still early for DAOs,

00:08:42.685 --> 00:08:44.771
and they certainly aren't for everything.

00:08:45.313 --> 00:08:47.732
They require a level of consensus building

00:08:47.774 --> 00:08:49.567
and might move slower than a company

00:08:49.609 --> 00:08:51.694
who has a boss
who can just call the shots.

00:08:52.153 --> 00:08:56.657
After all, ConstitutionDAO was outbid
at Sotheby's auction house

00:08:56.699 --> 00:08:58.201
by the CEO of Citadel.

00:08:58.618 --> 00:09:01.829
And some say the transparency
and decentralization

00:09:01.871 --> 00:09:04.999
made it hard for the DAO to coordinate
and win the auction.

00:09:07.001 --> 00:09:10.254
And while traditional corporate
structures are battle-tested,

00:09:10.296 --> 00:09:12.090
DAOs are a new type of entity

00:09:12.090 --> 00:09:15.551
that can find themselves
in uncharted regulatory waters.

00:09:16.511 --> 00:09:18.513
To help solve some of these issues,

00:09:18.554 --> 00:09:22.683
states like Wyoming are putting laws
on the books that recognize DAOs.

00:09:23.184 --> 00:09:27.522
And we actually used one of these laws
to buy our first piece of land at CityDAO,

00:09:27.563 --> 00:09:28.981
that's why it's in Wyoming.

00:09:31.234 --> 00:09:33.027
Once we work out the kinks,

00:09:33.027 --> 00:09:37.156
DAOs have the potential
to increase economic opportunity

00:09:37.198 --> 00:09:41.035
and allow more people to share
in the upsides of ownership.

00:09:42.036 --> 00:09:45.414
Things like real estate,
sports teams, fine art.

00:09:45.998 --> 00:09:48.167
These are things that would
typically be owned

00:09:48.167 --> 00:09:50.294
by a single, high net-worth individual

00:09:50.336 --> 00:09:53.714
that today DAOs are buying
and democratizing.

00:09:55.716 --> 00:10:00.763
Imagine if the next social network
or ride-hailing app were a DAO.

00:10:01.097 --> 00:10:04.725
And each time you posted valuable content
or put in late-nights driving,

00:10:04.725 --> 00:10:07.770
you got little pieces of ownership
in that platform.

00:10:08.396 --> 00:10:11.357
And since ownership means
voting rights in DAOs,

00:10:11.357 --> 00:10:14.986
you can use your new voting power
to propose changes to the platform

00:10:15.027 --> 00:10:17.989
if you think that there's a fairer
or better way to do things.

00:10:19.907 --> 00:10:22.702
Agriculture enabled us to live in cities.

00:10:23.786 --> 00:10:26.831
The internet let us share
information globally.

00:10:27.373 --> 00:10:31.210
And today, DAOs let us work together,

00:10:31.210 --> 00:10:32.503
trust each other

00:10:32.545 --> 00:10:34.922
and coordinate in a fairer way

00:10:34.922 --> 00:10:38.050
on larger-scale problems than ever before.

00:10:38.843 --> 00:10:42.889
And maybe a DAO can even build
the next great city.

00:10:43.431 --> 00:10:44.599
Thank you.

00:10:44.599 --> 00:10:48.895
(Applause)

